@host = http://localhost:5144

### 1. Sign in as the seeded admin (catalogue writes need the Admin role).
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "admin",
  "password": "Admin#1234",
  "tenantId: ""
}

### Copy "token" from the response above into a variable for every call below.
@token = PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### 2. List the seeded catalogue (cached: second call is served from Redis/L1 memory).
GET {{host}}/api/products?page=0&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Create a customer for the order.
POST {{host}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Persian Tools Co.",
  "address": "Tehran, Jomhouri Ave, No. 45",
  "email": "orders@persiantools.example"
}

### 4. Open a draft order in IRR. Keep the "id" and copy it into @orderId below.
@orderId = PASTE_ORDER_ID_HERE
@customerId = PASTE_CUSTOMER_ID_HERE

POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "currency": "IRR"
}

### 5. Add lines (any seeded product id from step 2).
@productId = PASTE_PRODUCT_ID_HERE

POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/lines
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "productId": "{{productId}}",
  "quantity": 2
}

### 6. Let the configured volume policy compute the discount (5% over 1,000,000 IRR).
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/discount/automatic
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Walk the state machine: place -> confirm -> ship -> deliver.
###    Each step returns the full document; each illegal jump returns 409 Problem Details.
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/place
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/ship
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/deliver
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. The finished document, with its ORD-000001 number and every timestamp.
GET {{host}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Negative checks worth trying on purpose:
###    401 — no token:   GET {{host}}/api/products
###    403 — clerk POSTs a product (login as salesclerk / Sales#1234)
###    409 — place an empty draft, or ship a draft
###    400 — {"userName":"x","password":"y"} to /api/auth/login (too-short user name)
###    401 — unknown user AND wrong password give byte-identical bodies
